  "goodToKnow": "Der Kaiserschnitt is a caesarean section: per Kaiserschnitt entbinden. Almost a third of babies in Germany are born this way. The name translates Latin sectio caesarea, linked by legend to Julius Caesar, though the link is probably false; Kaiser itself comes from Caesar. A natural birth is eine natürliche Geburt. Midwives are Hebammen. Plural: die Kaiserschnitte."
